MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* feat(identity): brand.icon as SSOT — header + gallery + og read one field

Today each fork hand-edits AppHeader.tsx to import a lucide icon + render
cogni/<slug> — the icon lives in component code, so surfacing it in the
operator gallery would hardcode it a SECOND time (split-brain).

Hoist the mark into repo-spec intent.brand.icon (a Lucide NAME) as the single
source. One curated registry (shared/brand/brandIcons) resolves name->component;
every surface reads it:
- AppHeader: server component renders brand.icon + cogni/<slug> from the field
  (forks stop hand-editing JSX — they set 2 repo-spec fields)
- opengraph-image: renders the big icon (gallery card + social og:image)
- agent.json: projects identity.brand.icon

Build-safety: AppHeader renders in statically-prerendered (public) pages where
serverEnv() has no runtime env and would throw (the same trap that broke the
og route). Added getBrandMark() — a build-safe repo-spec reader (env path first,
else walk up from cwd) with a neutral fallback — used ONLY by the header, so the
shared loadRepoSpec (node identity/scope/payments) is untouched.

node-template brand.icon = GitFork. thumbnail kept transitionally (gallery reads
it until the operator renders brand.icon directly).

* fix(identity): pass brandMark as prop — keep AppHeader client-safe

AppHeader is pulled into the client graph via the @/features/layout barrel, so
it can't import server-only repo-spec IO (node:fs). Read the brand in the server
(public) layout via getBrandMark() and pass the serializable {slug,icon,color}
as a prop; AppHeader resolves the icon name → component client-side.

---------

